OVERVIEW
--------
InterpolateChord fits a cubic B-spline to a given chord distribution and 
interpolates the chord at desired radii. It handles two distinct cases:
  1. Finite chord at tip (> 0.01): Uses PCHIP interpolation
  2. Near-zero chord at tip (<= 0.01): Uses B-spline curve fitting

FUNCTIONS IMPLEMENTED
--------------------

1. InterpolateChord(XR, XCoD, RG)
   Main function for chord interpolation
   
   INPUTS:
     XR   : array (Mx,) - Given radii r/R where chord is defined
     XCoD : array (Mx,) - Chord/diameter at XR  
     RG   : array (Mp,) - Radii r/R where interpolation is required
   
   OUTPUT:
     CoD  : array (Mp,) - Interpolated chord/diameter at RG
   
   LOGIC:
     - If |XR[-1] - 1| < 1e-4 AND XCoD[-1] > 0.01:
         Uses pchip1d() for direct interpolation
     - Else:
         Uses B-spline curve fitting:
         • Extends XR to r=1 if needed (with zero chord)
         • Creates symmetric blade outline (mirrors chord data)
         • Parameterizes using centripetal method: u = Σ√(Δr² + Δc²)
         • Computes knot vector using averaging method
         • Fits B-spline to (r,c) data pairs
         • Evaluates spline on fine grid (401 points)
         • Interpolates at desired RG using cubic interpolation
         • Applies offset for finite tip chord preservation

2. Bspline_basis(t, n_or_knot, k)
   Evaluates B-spline basis functions and derivatives
   
   INPUTS:
     t         : array (Mt,) - Parameter values where to evaluate
     n_or_knot : int or array - Either spline parameter n, or knot vector
     k         : int - Polynomial order (k=4 for cubic B-splines)
   
   OUTPUTS:
     B    : array (Mt, Ms) - Basis function values
     D1   : array (Mt, Ms) - First derivatives
     D2   : array (Mt, Ms) - Second derivatives  
     knot : array (Mk,)    - Knot vector
   
   ALGORITHM:
     • Cox-de Boor recursion formula
     • Handles repeated knots (clamped/open B-splines)
     • Computes derivatives using recursion on derivatives
     • Partition of unity: Sum B[i,:] = 1.0 for all i

3. pchip1d(x, v, xx)
   Piecewise Cubic Hermite Interpolating Polynomial
   
   INPUTS:
     x  : array (Nx,) - Data x-coordinates
     v  : array (Nx,) - Data values
     xx : array (Nxx,) - Query points
   
   OUTPUT:
     vv : array (Nxx,) - Interpolated values at xx
   
   FEATURES:
     • Shape-preserving: No overshoots between data points
     • C¹ continuous (value and first derivative continuous)
     • Uses Hermite basis functions: H1, H2, H3, H4
     • Slope estimation via pchipslopes()

4. pchipslopes(x, v)
   Computes shape-preserving slopes for PCHIP
   
   INPUTS:
     x : array (Nx,) - Data x-coordinates
     v : array (Nx,) - Data values
   
   OUTPUT:
     d : array (Nx,) - Derivatives at x
   
   ALGORITHM:
     • Interior points: Weighted harmonic mean if same sign
     • Endpoints: Three-point formula via pchipend()
     • Zero slope if adjacent segments have opposite signs

5. pchipend(h1, h2, del1, del2)
   Three-point formula for endpoint slopes
   
   INPUTS:
     h1   : float - Interval length near endpoint
     h2   : float - Next interval length
     del1 : float - Slope of near interval
     del2 : float - Slope of next interval
   
   OUTPUT:
     d : float - Derivative at endpoint
   
   FORMULA:
     d = ((2h1 + h2)·del1 - h1·del2) / (h1 + h2)
     With shape-preserving constraints

KEY IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS
--------------------------

1. B-spline Parameterization:
   - Centripetal method: u_i = Σ√(Δr² + Δc²) / total_length
   - Better than chord-length for blade shapes with varying curvature
   - Prevents parameter clustering

2. Knot Vector (Averaging Method):
   - Clamped/open B-spline: k repeated knots at ends
   - Interior knots: u[k+j] = mean(u[j+1:j+k-1])
   - Ensures interpolation at first/last control points

3. Symmetric Blade Outline:
   - Doubles data: (r, c) → (r, c) ∪ (r, -c)
   - Creates closed curve for spline fitting
   - Extracts upper half after fitting

4. Fine Grid Evaluation:
   - Evaluates spline on 401-point grid
   - Provides smooth representation for final interpolation
   - Cubic interpolation for RG values

5. Tip Chord Offset:
   - CoDoffset = (RG - RG[0]) / (1 - RG[0]) * CoDtip
   - Linear taper from hub to tip
   - Final: CoD = √(CoDraw² + CoDoffset²)

